' This is a demonstration of how to link in and handle shared files
' Before you can use this shared library, it has to be built. On Windows, use build_libs.ps1, and Linux and macOS use build_libs.sh.
' To see the options for building, use -h, or [--help/-help] depending on if the terminal is Powershell of bash. 

' As the compiled library output uses Unix style directory structures.
' The shared library will be outout to cx_shared_library_rect/demo_build/<preset name>/bin
' The the linker archive files will be placed in cx_shared_library_rect/demo_build/<preset name>/lib
' The lib directory will have a symbolic link the the actual shared library located in cx_shared_library_rect/demo_build/<preset name>/bin
'
' CMake will by design use linker archive files for linking, and the Cerberus implementation for CMake will use the symbolic link to copy the
' shared library. If the symbolic link is not there; then you should also include the actual path to the shared library binary to make sure that it's copied.

Import "interface/shared_lib_wrapper_rect.cpp"

